  "fetch": "git clone https://git.tartarus.org/simon/putty.git corpus/putty && git -C corpus/putty checkout 0.83",
  "_doc": "PuTTY is the first target here that is neither a game nor a 1990s DOS program: modern C99, a real Win32 GUI, and a build system that is itself data. It is a different kind of evidence -- Quake proves PRISM runs a renderer, this would prove it runs an application.",
  "_units": "COMPUTED, not transcribed: `node tools/putty-sources.mjs <executable>` reads every CMakeLists.txt in the tree and resolves the executable's libraries to files. PuTTY moves functions between units in utils/ constantly, so a hand-copied list would go stale within weeks. Regenerate rather than edit.",
