      "_generated": "wide.c is the wide-character corner of the C library. It is C rather than JavaScript because its contract is wchar_t's WIDTH, which the compiler knows and the runtime does not -- the same argument that makes mgl.c C.",
      "generated": [
        "src/env/wide.c",
        "src/env/inttypes.c",
        "src/env/win32-app.c"
      ],
      "unitDefines": {
        "windows/test/test_split_into_argv.c": {
          "TEST": "1"
        },
        "windows/utils/split_into_argv.c": {
          "_MSC_VER": "1400"
        }
      },
      "_msc_ver": "Not a workaround -- a CONFIGURATION, and PuTTY's source is what makes it necessary. split_into_argv.c:158 picks its behaviour with `#if _MSC_VER < 1400`, so a compiler that is not MSVC at all reads as older than Visual Studio 7 and gets the mod-3 quirk, while the TEST file -- which cannot see a macro defined inside a .c -- always expects the modern behaviour. Left alone the two halves disagree and 51 of 92 cases fail; the same would happen under MinGW. Saying _MSC_VER=1400 for this one unit says 'this compiler is not Visual Studio 7', which is true, and the two halves then agree exactly: 92/92."
    }
  },
  "_state": "IN PROGRESS -- this target does not build yet, and the file records where it stops rather than pretending otherwise. It now gets through defs.h, putty.h, windows/platform.h and most of terminal.c, and stops in the Win32 GUI headers (HFONT, LOGFONT, the WS_/HKEY_/CP_/BN_ constant families). That surface is MEASURED, not guessed: see docs/COMPAT.md.",
  "_why_win32": "The unix variant was resolved and compared rather than assumed: `--unix` pulls in GTK (unix/window.c, unifont.c, config-gtk.c), which is a larger and less useful surface than Win32's. So Windows is the cheaper platform here, which is the opposite of what it is for Quake.",
  "_generated_headers": "licence.h and version.h do not exist in the tree -- cmake/licence.cmake and Buildscr write them. `node tools/putty-generate.mjs` does the same, into corpus/putty-generated/, which is outside the source tree and gitignored; the include path picks it up from there. Run it after fetch.",
  "_have_strtoumax": "The same answer the resolver gives, in the form the PREPROCESSOR needs. CMake writes its feature tests into cmake.h; PuTTY reads HAVE_STRTOUMAX both to pick source files and, in windows/platform.h:128, to decide whether to define a static inline strtoumax over MSVC's _strtoui64. Answering only the first left that inline in every unit and cost 206 functions."
